    Fix Constant field with required=True raising ValueError (#2901)
    
    * Fix Constant field with required=True raising ValueError
    
    Constant.__init__ now sets load_default and dump_default after
    super().__init__() to avoid the required/load_default conflict
    check. Also overrides _validate_missing to skip the required
    check since a Constant always provides a value.
    
    The allow_none fix from #2894 is preserved by explicitly setting
    self.allow_none = True when the constant is None and allow_none
    was not provided.
    
    Fixes #2900.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
